WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.243 --> 00:00:03.580
- [Announcer] This is
the green-winged macaw.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.402
Aren't her colors stunning?

00:00:06.402 --> 00:00:08.767
So stunning, that the illegal parrot trade

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.474
has caused its population

00:00:10.474 --> 00:00:13.474
to decrease heavily in recent years.

00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:18.054
The green-winged macaw is
considered one of the largest

00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:22.478
macaw parrots, but also
one of the most docile.

00:00:22.478 --> 00:00:26.083
It is commonly referred
to as the gentle giant.

00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.439
They are very sweet,
affectionate, and friendly

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:30.990
with both humans and other birds.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.145
Maybe because of these easy-going ways,

00:00:33.145 --> 00:00:37.024
these birds have been known
to live upwards of 80 years.

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:40.544
They favor tropical forests
and swamps and savannas.

00:00:40.544 --> 00:00:42.873
Their habitat ranges
from Panama in the north,

00:00:42.873 --> 00:00:46.585
across South America, down
to Paraguay in the south.

00:00:46.585 --> 00:00:49.564
They feed on fruits,
seeds, berries, and nuts.

00:00:49.564 --> 00:00:51.889
Their incredibly powerful
beaks are capable

00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:54.897
of opening the hardest nuts and seeds.

00:00:54.897 --> 00:00:56.481
Along with poaching, their habitat

00:00:56.481 --> 00:00:59.667
has been shrinking considerably,
and in certain parts

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.558
where they used to be plentiful,

00:01:01.558 --> 00:01:04.710
they've become harder and harder to find.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.293
This is the green-winged macaw.

